{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1222225-hack-heralds-as-entering-level-template","id":1222225,"title":"[Hack] Heralds as entering level Template","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-26T06:17:18-07:00","id":1222225,"title":"[Hack] Heralds as entering level Template","content":"As I run my RPG club games, I uncovered that best is to give new players Lesser Template characters of the gameline for start and limited choices - and later on change them into proper gameline's Major Template, testing new players. In <b>Werewolf</b> I advise new players to start as Wolf-Blooded - make Mortal character, then choose one, maybe two Tells and we roll the with this PC in the game. After few sessions, as player is interested in continuing, we make him full Uratha in First Change.<br /> <br /> Now, as I slowly preparing <b>Beast</b> chronicle for another RPG club, I wonder if not using Heralds ( from <b>Beast Players Guide</b> ) in this way as Lesser Template. The problem is that in RAW Heralds are connected with particular Beast, not the Horror she is having. As I wanted more to make Heralds as entering to the proper Beast characters, I can simply make Heralds as 'champions' for particular Horror, preparing to be Devored.<br /> <br /> <b>But then comes another, larger dilemma - If making Heralds as proto-Beasts is even worthwhile, as really simplified character creation?</b> To choose powers for particular Herald we <i>already</i> need to have Horror for it in mind. You need to choose Life, Legend, Hunger, at least one Advanced Merit, Minor and Major Lair Traits. At this moment creating Herald is only less demanding than created proper Beast by not choosing Nightmares and Atavisms.<br /> <br /> <b>If making simplified Heralds temple doing it's service? Would loosing some of those choosing work for the characters that are 'dark cultists of particular Horror'?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T06:33:27-07:00","id":1222230,"title":"","content":"I don't understand your last question? Perhaps rephrase it? Honestly though, do what you want and think will work well. I just don't think Beasts are that hard to wrap your head around their mechanics in comparison if you're giving your homebrew heralds all these traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T07:18:20-07:00","id":1222238,"title":"","content":"Spawned the idea for a more limited lesser template here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=1222237#post1222237\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...37#post1222237</a><br /> <br /> I'm thinking: mortal + Atavism(s), maybe a Hunger (that they can use to recoup Satiety or Integrity, depending on which the template goes with). Mortal offspring of a Beast, so the Horror need not be present or fully developed to start. Might eventually inherit the full Horror in their own Devouring later (and transition into full template).<br /> <br /> Formidolosii, if I ever fully developed them, could serve for a basic Nightmares intro template. Or you could spin off a YAST (yet-anothet-sorcerer-take) as humans using Nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T07:28:53-07:00","id":1222243,"title":"","content":"I guess the &quot;cheaper&quot; way would be to run the to-be-Beasts as psychics/sorcerers, i.e. mortals with Supernatural Merits, whose theme fits with the Birthrights, Lair traits, Atavisms, and Nightmares they're soon going to get. Like giving Psychokinesis (Fire) to someone about to become a dragon and get the Dragonfire Atavism. Hey, psychics are Kin, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T08:36:41-07:00","id":1222259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1222225-hack-heralds-as-entering-level-template?p=1222243#post1222243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the &amp;quot;cheaper&amp;quot; way would be to run the to-be-Beasts as psychics/sorcerers, i.e. mortals with Supernatural Merits, whose theme fits with the Birthrights, Lair traits, Atavisms, and Nightmares they're soon going to get. Like giving Psychokinesis (Fire) to someone about to become a dragon and get the Dragonfire Atavism. Hey, psychics are Kin, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think wyrd wants something that still interacts with Beast's mechanics and possible themes, without the full template. Ghouls give a sample if discipline use before full Vampire, Proximi allow one to get used to Supernal magic without the full Mage options, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T12:49:47-07:00","id":1222290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1222225-hack-heralds-as-entering-level-template?p=1222243#post1222243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the &quot;cheaper&quot; way would be to run the to-be-Beasts as psychics/sorcerers, i.e. mortals with Supernatural Merits, whose theme fits with the Birthrights, Lair traits, Atavisms, and Nightmares they're soon going to get. Like giving Psychokinesis (Fire) to someone about to become a dragon and get the Dragonfire Atavism. Hey, psychics are Kin, so...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1222225-hack-heralds-as-entering-level-template?p=1222259#post1222259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think wyrd wants something that still interacts with Beast's mechanics and possible themes, without the full template. Ghouls give a sample if discipline use before full Vampire, Proximi allow one to get used to Supernal magic without the full Mage options, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I want some Lesser Template that is interacting with <b>Beast</b> setting at least, using some mechanics of it as good addition. Like Wolf-Blooded Tells in <b>Werewolf</b> - they split some mechanics of Uratha full template, giving a part ability to starting character, firmly in <b>WtF</b> setting as sort of resources all werewolf fight for. Using Supernatural Merits from<b> CoD Rulebook</b> can certainly be used for it - I literally have now new Wolf-Blooded character that play 'witch' that have one official Tell ( <i>Tongues</i> ) and two lower other Supernatural Merits. However...<br /> <br /> <b>I much more want to give players things that are easily to use, giving some part of future Begotten characters version 'prequeal'.</b> Thinking about it, making Heralds the pre-Devoured humans, may point to the Nightmares and maybe take part of Obcasus Rites. Much more 'cultists of dream Horrors' than fleshy sub-Beasts with non-the-less much more physical Atavisms.<br /> <br /> <b>The problem is with rewriting rules from Beasts template to 'Mortal+' version - Would using Willpower instead of Satiety be enough to work in mechanics framework?</b> Low Satiety effect would then work when character would have 1-2 Willpower points left?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-26-2018, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T13:54:08-07:00","id":1222297,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Atavisms and Nightmares are so much simpler than other splats' multi-step abilities, that I'm not sure any kind of slimmed down, entry level template is needed. If you do want to use Heralds for it... well, the book does say that they're automatically Devoured if their patron Inherits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T14:31:19-07:00","id":1222305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1222225-hack-heralds-as-entering-level-template?p=1222290#post1222290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>I much more want to give players things that are easily to use, giving some part of future Begotten characters version 'prequeal'.</b> Thinking about it, making Heralds the pre-Devoured humans, may point to the Nightmares and maybe take part of Obcasus Rites. Much more 'cultists of dream Horrors' than fleshy sub-Beasts with non-the-less much more physical Atavisms.<br /> <br /> <b>The problem is with rewriting rules from Beasts template to 'Mortal+' version - Would using Willpower instead of Satiety be enough to work in mechanics framework?</b> Low Satiety effect would then work when character would have 1-2 Willpower points left?</div> </div> </div> </div>Willpower varies too greatly to be reliable to track (as a ratio for <i>High</i> Satiety). It also seems more plentiful, so the Expenditure cost doesn't seem to have the same impact. Since Satiety is <i>supposed</i> to replace Integrity, why not just use that? At Integrity 7+, they get the HS effects. Once they start breaking, they lose the taste of power unless they keep investing in it. If costing a dot of Integrity is too much, treat voluntarily taking a Breaking Point as the SE cost. Actually, since Nightmares don't really cost anything to activate (other than the action), you might want to make them cost a Willpower for the Mortal+ characters.<br /> <br /> You should probably just make a separate template rather than Hacking the Herald one. More options, and easier to communicate with others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T15:02:15-07:00","id":1222313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1222225-hack-heralds-as-entering-level-template?p=1222305#post1222305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should probably just make a separate template rather than Hacking the Herald one. More options, and easier to communicate with others.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Progeny' and 'Hatchlings' present themselves as names. 'Worms', 'Infants' or 'Halfeaten' could be derogatory terms. It would depend, though, on the fluff of their metaphysics and their relationship with a Horror, Beasts and the Dark Dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T18:36:32-07:00","id":1222332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1222225-hack-heralds-as-entering-level-template?p=1222313#post1222313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'Progeny' and 'Hatchlings' present themselves as names. 'Worms', 'Infants' or 'Halfeaten' could be derogatory terms. It would depend, though, on the fluff of their metaphysics and their relationship with a Horror, Beasts and the Dark Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, considering the link to Nightmares, something like Phobos or Deimos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T01:20:27-07:00","id":1222366,"title":"","content":"Okay, here is what I hammer to this time. Thanks for ideas, especially <b>Vent0</b>.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Progeny ( Lesser Template )</span></b><br /> Before every Devouring are Dark Dreams of Primordial. Recurring, fear inducing, mind-bending nightmares, every day, every night. Often there is only few days between Horror induce his presence in subconscious of person, before creation of Beast \u2013 but sometimes it takes weeks, even months, some stories even takes about years - before Horror finally Devour human. In this transitional time, future Beast is receptive to Primordial Dream and fears of humanity. He even can shape Nightmares in others or participates in Obcasus Rites, if he focus enough. He is, for time being, Progeny of particular Horror \u2013 not a Beast yet, but not human also.<ul><li>Progeny gain <i>Unseen Sense: Primordial Dream</i> for free, or a permutation relating to their Horrors\u2019 Family Ties. Family Ties can be bought as Supernatural Merit. ( Probably 1 dot Merit? )</li> <li>Progeny starts with one Nightmare based on nature of Horror. Next Nightmares can be bought as Supernatural Merit. ( Probably 3 dot Merit? )</li> <li>For each rule saying about Satiety level use Progeny\u2019s Integrity as this trait. Satiety Expenditure is made for them as Breaking Point test,<b> not</b> direct lose dot of Integrity.</li> <li>Progeny can participate in Obcasus Rites and is counted as assisting Initiate or as cultist, deepening which better help the Rite performing</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-27-2018, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T04:57:24-07:00","id":1222377,"title":"","content":"Sounds nice, but maybe they shouldn\u2019t have Family Ties yet? It sounds like something meant for Beasts proper. <br /> <br /> Also, why the name Progeny? Yes, it was one of the suggestions, but the lore behind them doesn\u2019t point to them being distant relatives or descendents of Beasts/Horrors (unlike, say, Wolf-Blooded) Progeny of the Dark Mother? But that\u2019s a title every Primordial being has to claim, isn\u2019t it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T05:07:42-07:00","id":1222380,"title":"","content":"They are kind the &quot;child&quot; of the Horror that eventually will turn them into a Beast (where they become their own parent?). Although another good name is <b>Marked</b> - as in Marked-for-Devouring, or Mark-of-the-Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T05:15:15-07:00","id":1222382,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a less pleasant side to the Template should be added - maybe there's a way to use Progeny for hosts for Horrorspawn that makes them stronger?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T06:38:57-07:00","id":1222397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1222225-hack-heralds-as-entering-level-template?p=1222382#post1222382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps a less pleasant side to the Template should be added - maybe there's a way to use Progeny for hosts for Horrorspawn that makes them stronger?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, something like this?<ul><li><i>Progeny are sought out by Begotten not just because they can be nascent Beasts \u2013 but because they can become powerful tool, if Children of Dark Mother do not have qualms with humans morality. Using previous Progeny as body for Horrorspawn let it to decays two levels lower than normal. At Horrorspawn Potency it means 1 week till decay. At Potency 1 it\u2019s 6 months and Potency 2 it\u2019s 3 months.</i></li> </ul>So sacrifice your best monster cultists as vessel for yours new minor god\u2026 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1222225-hack-heralds-as-entering-level-template?p=1222377#post1222377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds nice, but maybe they shouldn\u2019t have Family Ties yet? It sounds like something meant for Beasts proper.</div> </div> </div> </div>I added possibility of Family Ties because some Nightmares need them. Also, I always thought that whole Kinship more originated from connection to Primordial Dream and fears of humanity, not that Horror per say have tentacle and a like. By this, with Progeny marked by Horror and it\u2019s Nightmares, I can think they can resonate with Family Ties, if they try hard enough. Rest of Kinship powers are outside of question for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T08:04:29-07:00","id":1222419,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about Obcasus rites. If they're close enough to a bunch of Beasts to be introduced to their religion and true nature, why haven't the Beasts helped Devour them yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T08:16:06-07:00","id":1222425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1222225-hack-heralds-as-entering-level-template?p=1222419#post1222419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure about Obcasus rites. If they're close enough to a bunch of Beasts to be introduced to their religion and true nature, why haven't the Beasts helped Devour them yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe can't or shouldn't until the Progeny is &quot;ripe&quot; enough?<br /> <br /> Which means one could also introduce what happens when the whole thing goes wrong, as a plot hook or new antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T09:23:41-07:00","id":1222444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1222225-hack-heralds-as-entering-level-template?p=1222419#post1222419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure about Obcasus rites. If they're close enough to a bunch of Beasts to be introduced to their religion and true nature, why haven't the Beasts helped Devour them yet?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1222225-hack-heralds-as-entering-level-template?p=1222425#post1222425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe can't or shouldn't until the Progeny is &quot;ripe&quot; enough?<br /> <br /> Which means one could also introduce what happens when the whole thing goes wrong, as a plot hook or new antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I feel that the ability to lead Obcasus Rites is something that should belong to Beasts. Perhaps the Progeny could have a Merit that allows them to be helpful to a Rite, but full Initiation should belong to the Begotten. However, as Vent0 says, it could be some kind of cultural thing. <br /> <br /> One thing I kind of like the idea of is for Progeny to have, instead of a Horror, a Seed - the beginning of a story. It's a theme, or something like that, that if they act in accordance with it - i.e. do something similar to Feeding for Beasts - it acts as a beacon for Horrors. Mechanically, acting in accordance with your Seed would allow you to roll however many dice (I'm not sure of the pool) and accumulate that many successes towards attracting a Horror, as a kind of weird Extended Action. I'm not sure what the requirement would be, or if the Progeny should have any kind of conscious control of this at all, beyond acting or not acting in accordance with their Seed, but I do like the idea of the Progeny being kind of like kids in an orphanage, trying to look as good as they can for prospective parents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T09:40:17-07:00","id":1222448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1222225-hack-heralds-as-entering-level-template?p=1222444#post1222444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I feel that the ability to lead Obcasus Rites is something that should belong to Beasts. Perhaps the Progeny could have a Merit that allows them to be helpful to a Rite, but full Initiation should belong to the Begotten. However, as Vent0 says, it could be some kind of cultural thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Progeny <b>do not</b> lead in Rites. They only can work as better of two Trappings - assistant or cultist. They are usefull, but not making proper Rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-27-2018, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}